{"title":"1998 JBMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_JBMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prove that the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/b/4fb9deda28dd806ab7c5291115fb23684e753144.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underbrace{111\\ldots 11}_{1997}\\underbrace{22\\ldots 22}_{1998}5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"151\" height=\"34\" /> (which has 1997 of 1-s and 1998 of 2-s) is a perfect square.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 JBMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_JBMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> be a convex pentagon such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/1/581644f838eda95bac5bb30309012d9e684cabc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AE=CD=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"167\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f62e5a436b21e7de6c25096940a7295c0bda4866.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC=\\angle DEA=90^\\circ$\" width=\"184\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/e/08eff57c444eeae7b3ae3d190d6582c1d0afcbf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC+DE=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" />. Compute the area of the pentagon.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 JBMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_JBMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all pairs of positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98ac839a2ad0030079cd9730649546627b3937a9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^y = y^{x - y}.\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 JBMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_JBMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Do[es] there exist 16 three digit numbers, using only three different digits in all, so that the all numbers give different residues when divided by 16?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1998 JBMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_JBMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_JBMO\" title=\"1998 JBMO\">1998 JBMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13_contests\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_JBMO_Problems\" title=\"1997 JBMO Problems\">1997 JBMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_JBMO_Problems\" title=\"1999 JBMO Problems\">1999 JBMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_JBMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 JBMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_JBMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 JBMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_JBMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 JBMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_JBMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1998 JBMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JBMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" title=\"JBMO Problems and Solutions, with authors\"> All JBMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p><br />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017121107\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 76/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 828/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 68/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1283/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    9.298      1 Template:JBMO_box\n100.00%    9.298      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16652:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017121107 and revision id 136287. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}